  "content": [
    {
      "type": "thinking",
      "thinking": "I'm planning the full HTML structure, covering validation rules for adding people and expenses—trimmed unique names, positive amounts with at most two decimals, payer selection, and split checkboxes defaulting to checked—plus how to handle cents rounding and remainder distribution among selected people in the order they joined the trip.\n\nNow I'm working out balances as paid minus share, and a greedy settle-up algorithm that sorts debtors and creditors to produce the minimum number of transfers. I'm also deciding on formatting money with Intl.NumberFormat for CAD, persisting state in localStorage, and handling empty states and responsive accessible layout down to 360px.\n\nFor visual personality I'm choosing Fraunces for display type and IBM Plex Sans for body text with tabular numerals, paired with a warm off-white background, deep harbour blue for primary text, and a muted signal red/teal pairing for negative/positive balances, checking contrast ratios as I go.\n\nI'm checking WCAG contrast ratios for the signal red and harbour blue against white backgrounds by computing relative luminance manually, confirming both clear AA thresholds for text and button use. Now I'm sketching the grid layout — header plus a two-column arrangement for people/add-expense on one side and the expense list, balances, and settle-up on the other, collapsing to a single column on mobile — and defining the regex-based amount validation that converts valid decimal strings into integer cents.\n\nI decide to use a text input with inputmode=\"decimal\" instead of a number input to preserve exactly what the user typed and avoid number-input quirks, then sketch the expense data shape storing id, description, cents, payer, and the split array ordered by the people list so share calculations stay consistent.\n\nFor dividing costs, I compute a base share via integer division and distribute the remainder cents to the first few people in order so totals reconcile exactly. For settling up, I calculate each person's balance as paid minus owed, then greedily match creditors to debtors (sorted by amount) to minimize the number of transfers, which keeps transactions to at most n-1. I also plan to only render the error element when there's actually an error to show, rather than always rendering it hidden.\n\nI'll keep expense form errors simple by surfacing just the first validation issue rather than listing everything, and mark the relevant inputs as aria-invalid for accessibility. The render function will need to redraw the people list, payer dropdown, and split checkboxes while preserving which people are currently selected, defaulting new additions to selected as well.\n\nFor deletion I'll just remove expenses directly without a confirmation step. For empty states, I'm drafting friendly placeholder text for each section—people, expenses, balances, and settling up—so the app doesn't feel broken before any data exists.\n\nThe expense form should stay enabled even without people, but show a message prompting the user to add someone first; attempting to submit with no people should fail validation. I'll persist state under a single localStorage key storing people and expenses together, make sure accessibility basics like labels and focus outlines are in place, and add an optional \"Clear trip\" reset button with a confirm dialog in the header, alongside a dark header band with the Even Keel wordmark and tagline.\n\nNow I'm picking the color palette: a warm off-white background, white cards with a subtle border, Fraunces for headings, and tabular numerals for figures. I'm verifying contrast ratios for accent colors—checking that the teal green used for positive amounts and the muted gray text both meet accessibility contrast thresholds against the white background.\n\nNow I'm sketching the page structure: a topbar with branding and a reset button, and a main grid with cards for the people form/list, expense form, and results list.\n\nFor the layout, I'm using a two-column CSS grid on desktop (People/Add Expense on the left, Expenses/Balances/Settle on the right), collapsing to a single stacked column with named grid-template-areas for mobile.\n\nFor the JS, I'm setting up a currency formatter for CAD and planning out an amount-parsing helper.\n\nWriting amount validation logic...\n\nI'll need an HTML escaping helper, then build out the expense list items showing description, amount, payer, and split participants, with a delete button labeled per expense. For balances I'll show each person's name with colored owed/owes/even status, and for settling up I'll format transfer suggestions like \"Ben pays Ana $12.00\" before assembling everything together.\n\n",
      "signature": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en-CA\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Even Keel — split trip costs</title>\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,500;9..144,600&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n<style>\n  :root{\n    --harbour:#1F3A4D;\n    --harbour-deep:#15293A;\n    --harbour-tint:#E6EDF2;\n    --signal:#C2462B;\n    --signal-deep:#A33A22;\n    --signal-tint:#FBEAE5;\n    --keel:#2C6E5A;\n    --keel-tint:#E3F0EB;\n    --sand:#F4F1EB;\n    --paper:#FFFFFF;\n    --line:#DDD6CB;\n    --line-strong:#B9AFA0;\n    --ink:#1A2733;\n    --muted:#5B6B76;\n    --radius:10px;\n    --focus:0 0 0 3px #fff, 0 0 0 6px var(--signal);\n    font-size:16px;\n  }\n  *{box-sizing:border-box}\n  html,body{margin:0;padding:0}\n  body{\n    font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;\n    color:var(--ink);\n    background:var(--sand);\n    line-height:1.5;\n    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;\n  }\n  h1,h2,h3{font-family:\"Fraunces\",Georgia,serif;font-weight:600;margin:0;letter-spacing:-0.01em}\n  p{margin:0}\n  button,input,select{font:inherit;color:inherit}\n  :focus-visible{outline:none;box-shadow:var(--focus);border-radius:6px}\n  .wrap{width:100%;max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px}\n  @media (min-width:720px){.wrap{padding:0 28px}}\n\n  /* top bar */\n  .topbar{background:var(--harbour);color:#fff;border-bottom:4px solid var(--signal)}\n  .topbar .wrap{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;padding-top:22px;padding-bottom:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n  .brand{font-family:\"Fraunces\",Georgia,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:1.9rem;line-height:1;letter-spacing:-0.02em}\n  .brand span{display:inline-block;width:.5em;height:.5em;border-radius:50%;background:var(--signal);margin-left:.18em;vertical-align:baseline}\n  .tag{color:#C9D5DE;font-size:.95rem;margin-top:6px}\n  .topbar button{background:transparent;color:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.45);padding:8px 14px;border-radius:999px;cursor:pointer;font-size:.9rem}\n  .topbar button:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1);border-color:#fff}\n  .topbar :focus-visible{box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--harbour),0 0 0 6px #fff}\n\n  /* layout */\n  main{padding:24px 0 56px}\n  .grid{display:grid;gap:18px;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);\n    grid-template-areas:\"people\" \"add\" \"balances\" \"settle\" \"expenses\"}\n  @media (min-width:860px){\n    .grid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,5fr) minmax(0,7fr);gap:22px;\n      grid-template-areas:\"people expenses\" \"add expenses\" \"add balances\" \"add settle\"}\n  }\n  .card{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:20px;min-width:0;align-self:start}\n  @media (min-width:720px){.card{padding:24px}}\n  .card.people{grid-area:people}\n  .card.add{grid-area:add}\n  .card.expenses{grid-area:expenses}\n  .card.balances{grid-area:balances}\n  .card.settle{grid-area:settle}\n  .card-head{display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:14px;padding-bottom:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}\n  .card-head h2{font-size:1.35rem;color:var(--harbour)}\n  .count{color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}\n  .lead{color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:14px}\n\n  /* forms */\n  label,legend{display:block;font-weight:500;font-size:.92rem;color:var(--harbour);margin-bottom:6px}\n  .field{margin-bottom:14px}\n  .hint{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;margin-top:4px}\n  input[type=text],select{\n    width:100%;padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;background:#fff;min-height:44px\n  }\n  input[type=text]:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{border-color:var(--harbour);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px #fff,0 0 0 5px var(--harbour);border-radius:8px}\n  input[aria-invalid=true]{border-color:var(--signal);background:#fffaf8}\n  .prefix{position:relative}\n  .prefix span{position:absolute;left:12px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);color:var(--muted);pointer-events:none}\n  .prefix input{padding-left:28px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n  .row{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start}\n  .row .field{flex:1 1 auto;margin-bottom:0}\n  .row .btn{margin-top:27px}\n  fieldset{border:0;padding:0;margin:0}\n  .checks{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}\n  .checks label{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin:0;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:999px;background:#fff;cursor:pointer;font-weight:500;color:var(--ink);min-height:40px}\n  .checks label:has(input:checked){background:var(--harbour-tint);border-color:var(--harbour)}\n  .checks label:has(input:focus-visible){box-shadow:var(--focus)}\n  .checks input{width:18px;height:18px;margin:0;accent-color:var(--harbour)}\n  .checks-empty,.empty{color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;padding:14px;border:1px dashed var(--line-strong);border-radius:8px;background:var(--sand)}\n  .btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;min-height:44px;padding:10px 18px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid transparent;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap}\n  .btn-primary{background:var(--harbour);color:#fff}\n  .btn-primary:hover{background:var(--harbour-deep)}\n  .btn-signal{background:var(--signal);color:#fff;width:100%}\n  .btn-signal:hover{background:var(--signal-deep)}\n  .btn-quiet{background:transparent;color:var(--harbour);border-color:var(--line-strong);padding:6px 12px;min-height:36px;font-size:.88rem;font-weight:500}\n  .btn-quiet:hover{background:var(--signal-tint);color:var(--signal-deep);border-color:var(--signal)}\n  .error{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;margin-top:12px;padding:10px 12px;border-left:3px solid var(--signal);background:var(--signal-tint);color:#7E2D1A;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;font-size:.93rem}\n  .error::before{content:\"\";flex:none;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--signal);margin-top:.5em}\n\n  /* lists */\n  ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}\n  .people-list{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}\n  .people-list li{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:7px 12px 7px 8px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;background:var(--sand);font-weight:500}\n  .avatar{width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--harbour);color:#fff;display:inline-grid;place-items:center;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;font-family:\"Fraunces\",Georgia,serif}\n  .expense-list li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;gap:4px 12px;padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}\n  .expense-list li:last-child{border-bottom:0;padding-bottom:0}\n  .expense-list li:first-child{padding-top:0}\n  .exp-desc{font-weight:600;font-size:1.02rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\n  .exp-amt{font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap;text-align:right;font-size:1.02rem}\n  .exp-meta{grid-column:1 / -1;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\n  .exp-meta strong{color:var(--ink);font-weight:500}\n  .exp-actions{grid-column:1 / -1;margin-top:6px}\n  .bal-list li{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:11px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}\n  .bal-list li:last-child{border-bottom:0}\n  .bal-name{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-weight:500;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\n  .bal-amt{text-align:right;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n  .bal-amt b{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem}\n  .bal-amt small{color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}\n  .pos b{color:var(--keel)}\n  .neg b{color:var(--signal)}\n  .zero b{color:var(--muted)}\n  .transfer-list li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;align-items:center;gap:6px 12px;padding:12px 14px;margin-bottom:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--sand)}\n  .transfer-list li:last-child{margin-bottom:0}\n  .transfer-list .who{font-weight:500;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\n  .transfer-list .who .arrow{color:var(--signal);margin:0 6px;font-weight:600}\n  .transfer-list .amt{font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap;color:var(--harbour)}\n  .even{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;padding:14px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--keel-tint);color:#1F4F42;font-weight:500}\n  .even::before{content:\"\";flex:none;width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--keel)}\n  .sr-only{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);white-space:nowrap;border:0}\n  .foot{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;text-align:center;margin-top:36px}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header class=\"topbar\">\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n    <div>\n      <p class=\"brand\">Even Keel<span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></p>\n      <p class=\"tag\">Log what each of you paid. We'll work out how to end up even.</p>\n    </div>\n    <button type=\"button\" id=\"reset-trip\">Start a new trip</button>\n  </div>\n</header>\n\n<main data-testid=\"app\" class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"grid\">\n\n    <section class=\"card people\" aria-labelledby=\"people-h\">\n      <div class=\"card-head\">\n        <h2 id=\"people-h\">Who's on the trip</h2>\n        <p class=\"count\" id=\"people-count\"></p>\n      </div>\n      <form id=\"person-form\" novalidate>\n        <div class=\"row\">\n          <div class=\"field\">\n            <label for=\"person-name\">Name</label>\n            <input type=\"text\" id=\"person-name\" data-testid=\"person-name\" autocomplete=\"off\" placeholder=\"e.g. Ana\" maxlength=\"40\">\n          </div>\n          <button type=\"submit\" class=\"btn btn-primary\" data-testid=\"add-person\">Add</button>\n        </div>\n        <div id=\"person-error\"></div>\n      </form>\n      <div id=\"people-list\" style=\"margin-top:16px\"></div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"card add\" aria-labelledby=\"add-h\">\n      <div class=\"card-head\">\n        <h2 id=\"add-h\">Log an expense</h2>\n      </div>\n      <form id=\"expense-form\" novalidate>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"expense-desc\">What was it for?</label>\n          <input type=\"text\" id=\"expense-desc\" data-testid=\"expense-desc\" autocomplete=\"off\" placeholder=\"e.g. Groceries, ferry tickets\" maxlength=\"80\">\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"expense-amount\">Amount (CAD)</label>\n          <div class=\"prefix\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">$</span>\n            <input type=\"text\" id=\"expense-amount\" data-testid=\"expense-amount\" inputmode=\"decimal\" autocomplete=\"off\" placeholder=\"0.00\">\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"hint\">Dollars and cents, up to two decimal places.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"field\">\n          <label for=\"expense-payer\">Who paid?</label>\n          <select id=\"expense-payer\" data-testid=\"expense-payer\"></select>\n        </div>\n        <fieldset class=\"field\">\n          <legend>Split between</legend>\n          <div id=\"expense-split\" class=\"checks\" data-testid=\"expense-split\"></div>\n          <p class=\"hint\" id=\"split-hint\">Shared equally. Leftover cents go to the people who joined the trip first.</p>\n        </fieldset>\n        <button type=\"submit\" class=\"btn btn-signal\" data-testid=\"add-expense\">Add expense</button>\n        <div id=\"expense-error\"></div>\n      </form>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"card expenses\" aria-labelledby=\"exp-h\">\n      <div class=\"card-head\">\n        <h2 id=\"exp-h\">Expenses</h2>\n        <p class=\"count\" id=\"expense-total\"></p>\n      </div>\n      <div id=\"expense-list\"></div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"card balances\" aria-labelledby=\"bal-h\">\n      <div class=\"card-head\">\n        <h2 id=\"bal-h\">Where everyone stands</h2>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"lead\">What each of you paid, minus your share of the costs.</p>\n      <div id=\"balance-list\"></div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"card settle\" aria-labelledby=\"settle-h\">\n      <div class=\"card-head\">\n        <h2 id=\"settle-h\">Settle up</h2>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"lead\">The fewest transfers that bring everyone back to zero.</p>\n      <div id=\"transfer-list\"></div>\n    </section>\n\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"foot\">Saved on this device. Nothing is sent anywhere.</p>\n</main>\n\n<script>\n(function(){\n  'use strict';\n  const STORE_KEY = 'evenkeel.v1';\n  const fmt = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-CA', { style:'currency', currency:'CAD' });\n  const money = c => fmt.format(c / 100);\n  const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);\n  const esc = s => String(s).replace(/[&<>\"']/g, ch => ({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;',\"'\":'&#39;'}[ch]));\n\n  let state = { people: [], expenses: [] };\n  // Names the user has explicitly unchecked in the split (so new people default to checked).\n  let splitUnchecked = new Set();\n\n  function load(){\n    try {\n      const raw = localStorage.getItem(STORE_KEY);\n      if (!raw) return;\n      const data = JSON.parse(raw);\n      if (data && Array.isArray(data.people) && Array.isArray(data.expenses)) {\n        state.people = data.people.filter(p => typeof p === 'string');\n        state.expenses = data.expenses.filter(e => e && typeof e.desc === 'string' && Number.isInteger(e.cents) && typeof e.payer === 'string' && Array.isArray(e.split));\n      }\n    } catch (e) { /* start fresh */ }\n  }\n  function save(){\n    try { localStorage.setItem(STORE_KEY, JSON.stringify(state)); } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- helpers ---------- */\n  function initials(name){\n    const parts = name.trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    return (parts[0][0] + (parts.length > 1 ? parts[parts.length-1][0] : '')).toUpperCase();\n  }\n  function listNames(names){\n    if (names.length === 0) return '';\n    if (names.length === 1) return esc(names[0]);\n    return names.slice(0, -1).map(esc).join(', ') + ' and ' + esc(names[names.length-1]);\n  }\n  function orderByTrip(names){\n    const set = new Set(names);\n    return state.people.filter(p => set.has(p));\n  }\n  // Equal split in integer cents; leftover cents go one each in trip order.\n  function shares(cents, splitNames){\n    const ordered = orderByTrip(splitNames);\n    const n = ordered.length;\n    const base = Math.floor(cents / n);\n    const rem = cents % n;\n    const out = {};\n    ordered.forEach((name, i) => { out[name] = base + (i < rem ? 1 : 0); });\n    return out;\n  }\n  function balances(){\n    const bal = {};\n    state.people.forEach(p => bal[p] = 0);\n    state.expenses.forEach(e => {\n      if (e.payer in bal) bal[e.payer] += e.cents;\n      const s = shares(e.cents, e.split);\n      for (const name in s) if (name in bal) bal[name] -= s[name];\n    });\n    return bal;\n  }\n  function settle(bal){\n    const creditors = [], debtors = [];\n    for (const name in bal) {\n      if (bal[name] > 0) creditors.push({ name, amt: bal[name] });\n      else if (bal[name] < 0) debtors.push({ name, amt: -bal[name] });\n    }\n    creditors.sort((a,b) => b.amt - a.amt || a.name.localeCompare(b.name));\n    debtors.sort((a,b) => b.amt - a.amt || a.name.localeCompare(b.name));\n    const transfers = [];\n    let i = 0, j = 0;\n    while (i < debtors.length && j < creditors.length) {\n      const d = debtors[i], c = creditors[j];\n      const amt = Math.min(d.amt, c.amt);\n      transfers.push({ from: d.name, to: c.name, cents: amt });\n      d.amt -= amt; c.amt -= amt;\n      if (d.amt === 0) i++;\n      if (c.amt === 0) j++;\n    }\n    return transfers;\n  }\n  function parseAmount(raw){\n    const s = raw.trim().replace(/^\\$/, '').replace(/,/g, '');\n    if (s === '') return { error: 'Enter an amount.' };\n    if (!/^(\\d+(\\.\\d*)?|\\.\\d+)$/.test(s)) return { error: 'Enter the amount in dollars and cents, like 42.50.' };\n    const [w = '0', f = ''] = s.split('.');\n    if (f.length > 2) return { error: 'Amounts can have at most two decimal places.' };\n    const cents = parseInt(w || '0', 10) * 100 + parseInt((f + '00').slice(0, 2), 10);\n    if (!Number.isFinite(cents) || cents > 1e13) return { error: 'That amount is too large.' };\n    if (cents <= 0) return { error: 'The amount needs to be more than $0.00.' };\n    return { cents };\n  }\n  function showError(container, msg){\n    container.innerHTML = msg ? '<p class=\"error\" data-testid=\"form-error\" role=\"alert\">' + esc(msg) + '</p>' : '';\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- rendering ---------- */\n  function renderPeople(){\n    const n = state.people.length;\n    $('people-count').textContent = n ? (n === 1 ? '1 person' : n + ' people') : '';\n    const el = $('people-list');\n    if (!n) {\n      el.innerHTML = '<p class=\"empty\">No one's here yet. Add the people on the trip, starting with yourself.</p>';\n      return;\n    }\n    el.innerHTML = '<ul class=\"people-list\" aria-label=\"People on the trip\">' +\n      state.people.map(p => '<li data-testid=\"person\"><span class=\"avatar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">' + esc(initials(p)) + '</span>' + esc(p) + '</li>').join('') +\n      '</ul>';\n  }\n  function renderExpenseForm(){\n    const sel = $('expense-payer');\n    const prev = sel.value;\n    if (!state.people.length) {\n      sel.innerHTML = '<option value=\"\">Add a person first</option>';\n      sel.disabled = true;\n    } else {\n      sel.disabled = false;\n      sel.innerHTML = state.people.map(p => '<option value=\"' + esc(p) + '\">' + esc(p) + '</option>').join('');\n      sel.value = state.people.includes(prev) ? prev : state.people[0];\n    }\n    const split = $('expense-split');\n    if (!state.people.length) {\n      split.innerHTML = '<p class=\"checks-empty\">Once you've added people, you can choose who shares this cost.</p>';\n    } else {\n      split.innerHTML = state.people.map((p, i) => {\n        const id = 'split-' + i;\n        const checked = splitUnchecked.has(p) ? '' : ' checked';\n        return '<label for=\"' + id + '\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"' + id + '\" name=\"split\" value=\"' + esc(p) + '\"' + checked + '>' + esc(p) + '</label>';\n      }).join('');\n    }\n  }\n  function renderExpenses(){\n    const el = $('expense-list');\n    const total = state.expenses.reduce((s, e) => s + e.cents, 0);\n    $('expense-total').textContent = state.expenses.length ? money(total) + ' total' : '';\n    if (!state.expenses.length) {\n      el.innerHTML = '<p class=\"empty\">Nothing logged yet. When someone pays for something, add it here and it'll show up for everyone.</p>';\n      return;\n    }\n    const items = state.expenses.slice().reverse().map(e => {\n      const splitOrdered = orderByTrip(e.split);\n      const everyone = splitOrdered.length === state.people.length && state.people.length > 1;\n      return '<li data-testid=\"expense\" data-id=\"' + e.id + '\">' +\n        '<p class=\"exp-desc\">' + esc(e.desc) + '</p>' +\n        '<p class=\"exp-amt\">' + money(e.cents) + '</p>' +\n        '<p class=\"exp-meta\">Paid by <strong>' + esc(e.payer) + '</strong> · split between <strong>' + listNames(splitOrdered) + '</strong>' + (everyone ? ' (everyone)' : '') + '</p>' +\n        '<div class=\"exp-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-quiet\" data-testid=\"delete-expense\" data-id=\"' + e.id + '\" aria-label=\"Remove ' + esc(e.desc) + '\">Remove</button></div>' +\n        '</li>';\n    }).join('');\n    el.innerHTML = '<ul class=\"expense-list\" aria-label=\"Expenses, newest first\">' + items + '</ul>';\n  }\n  function renderBalances(){\n    const el = $('balance-list');\n    const tl = $('transfer-list');\n    if (!state.people.length) {\n      el.innerHTML = '<p class=\"empty\">Balances appear once there are people on the trip.</p>';\n      tl.innerHTML = '<p class=\"empty\">Nothing to settle yet.</p>';\n      return;\n    }\n    const bal = balances();\n    el.innerHTML = '<ul class=\"bal-list\">' + state.people.map(p => {\n      const c = bal[p];\n      const cls = c > 0 ? 'pos' : c < 0 ? 'neg' : 'zero';\n      const word = c > 0 ? 'is owed' : c < 0 ? 'owes' : 'even';\n      const shown = c > 0 ? '+' + money(c) : c < 0 ? '−' + money(-c) : money(0);\n      return '<li data-testid=\"balance\" data-person=\"' + esc(p) + '\" data-cents=\"' + c + '\" class=\"' + cls + '\">' +\n        '<span class=\"bal-name\"><span class=\"avatar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">' + esc(initials(p)) + '</span>' + esc(p) + '</span>' +\n        '<span class=\"bal-amt\"><b>' + shown + '</b><small>' + word + '</small></span></li>';\n    }).join('') + '</ul>';\n\n    if (!state.expenses.length) {\n      tl.innerHTML = '<p class=\"empty\">Nothing to settle yet. Log an expense and the transfers appear here.</p>';\n      return;\n    }\n    const transfers = settle(bal);\n    if (!transfers.length) {\n      tl.innerHTML = '<p class=\"even\">You're all even. Nothing to pay back.</p>';\n      return;\n    }\n    tl.innerHTML = '<ul class=\"transfer-list\" aria-label=\"Transfers to settle up\">' + transfers.map(t =>\n      '<li data-testid=\"transfer\" data-from=\"' + esc(t.from) + '\" data-to=\"' + esc(t.to) + '\" data-cents=\"' + t.cents + '\">' +\n      '<span class=\"who\">' + esc(t.from) + '<span class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span><span class=\"sr-only\"> pays </span>' + esc(t.to) + '</span>' +\n      '<span class=\"amt\">' + money(t.cents) + '</span></li>'\n    ).join('') + '</ul>';\n  }\n  function render(){\n    renderPeople();\n    renderExpenseForm();\n    renderExpenses();\n    renderBalances();\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- events ---------- */\n  $('person-form').addEventListener('submit', ev => {\n    ev.preventDefault();\n    const input = $('person-name');\n    const name = input.value.trim();\n    let error = '';\n    if (!name) error = 'Enter a name before adding someone.';\n    else if (state.people.some(p => p.toLowerCase() === name.toLowerCase())) error = '\"' + name + '\" is already on the trip. Names need to be unique, ignoring capital letters.';\n    if (error) {\n      input.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');\n      showError($('person-error'), error);\n      input.focus();\n      return;\n    }\n    input.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');\n    showError($('person-error'), '');\n    state.people.push(name);\n    save();\n    render();\n    input.value = '';\n    input.focus();\n  });\n  $('person-name').addEventListener('input', () => {\n    $('person-name').removeAttribute('aria-invalid');\n    showError($('person-error'), '');\n  });\n\n  $('expense-split').addEventListener('change', ev => {\n    const cb = ev.target;\n    if (cb && cb.type === 'checkbox') {\n      if (cb.checked) splitUnchecked.delete(cb.value); else splitUnchecked.add(cb.value);\n    }\n  });\n\n  $('expense-form').addEventListener('submit', ev => {\n    ev.preventDefault();\n    const descEl = $('expense-desc'), amtEl = $('expense-amount'), payerEl = $('expense-payer');\n    [descEl, amtEl].forEach(el => el.removeAttribute('aria-invalid'));\n    const errBox = $('expense-error');\n    if (!state.people.length) {\n      showError(errBox, 'Add at least one person to the trip before logging an expense.');\n      return;\n    }\n    const desc = descEl.value.trim();\n    const amount = parseAmount(amtEl.value);\n    const payer = payerEl.value;\n    const split = Array.from($('expense-split').querySelectorAll('input[type=checkbox]:checked')).map(cb => cb.value);\n    const problems = [];\n    if (!desc) { problems.push('Say what the expense was for.'); descEl.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true'); }\n    if (amount.error) { problems.push(amount.error); amtEl.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true'); }\n    if (!state.people.includes(payer)) problems.push('Choose who paid.');\n    if (!split.length) problems.push('Choose at least one person to split it between.');\n    if (problems.length) {\n      showError(errBox, problems.join(' '));\n      const first = !desc ? descEl : amount.error ? amtEl : !state.people.includes(payer) ? payerEl : $('expense-split').querySelector('input');\n      if (first) first.focus();\n      return;\n    }\n    showError(errBox, '');\n    state.expenses.push({ id: Date.now().toString(36) + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 7), desc, cents: amount.cents, payer, split: orderByTrip(split) });\n    save();\n    descEl.value = '';\n    amtEl.value = '';\n    splitUnchecked = new Set();\n    render();\n    descEl.focus();\n  });\n  ['expense-desc', 'expense-amount'].forEach(id => $(id).addEventListener('input', () => {\n    $(id).removeAttribute('aria-invalid');\n    showError($('expense-error'), '');\n  }));\n\n  $('expense-list').addEventListener('click', ev => {\n    const btn = ev.target.closest('[data-testid=\"delete-expense\"]');\n    if (!btn) return;\n    state.expenses = state.expenses.filter(e => e.id !== btn.dataset.id);\n    save();\n    render();\n    $('exp-h').focus && $('exp-h').setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');\n    $('exp-h').focus();\n  });\n\n  $('reset-trip').addEventListener('click', () => {\n    if (!state.people.length && !state.expenses.length) return;\n    if (!confirm('Start a new trip? This clears everyone and every expense on this device.')) return;\n    state = { people: [], expenses: [] };\n    splitUnchecked = new Set();\n    save();\n    render();\n    $('person-name').focus();\n  });\n\n  load();\n  render();\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>"
